The **Rule Validator** tab allows validation rules to be applied to the target record before the DocSolutions configuration is completed. Set **Use Rule Validator** to **Yes** and enter the rule definition in **Rule Validator Json**.

The JSON is evaluated in two phases:

1. The `when` condition group determines whether the validations apply. If it is omitted or contains no conditions, it evaluates to true. Conditions use `and` by default; set `logic` to `or` to require at least one condition to be true.
2. If `when` is false, `otherwise` controls the result. The default is `success`, so the configuration continues and `validations` are not evaluated. Set it to `error` to stop the configuration and optionally provide `otherwiseMessage`.
3. If `when` is true, the rules in `validations` are evaluated. All failed validations are returned together; if at least one fails, the configuration is skipped.
